                                "text": "1891, Thomas Hardy, Tess of the d’Urbervilles, Phase the Fourth, Chapter 25,\n[…] since he had last shared in the Vicarage life it had grown even more distinctly foreign to his own than usual. Its transcendental aspirations—still unconsciously based on the geocentric view of things, a zenithal paradise, a nadiral hell—were as foreign to his own as if they had been the dreams of people on another planet."
